1:[["$","section",null,{"className":"intro","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"RISKSTRIKER / PLATFORM IN DEVELOPMENT"}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"What can the agent do when things go wrong?"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"lead","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"We're building RiskStriker to test consequential AI agents in context, measure downstream impact and verify whether controls contain it."}]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"section","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-head","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-label","children":"THE METHOD"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":["Context. Failure.",["$","br",null,{}],"Consequence. Control."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The proposed assessment follows the complete system, from the agent's authority to the actions that reach downstream services."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid3","children":[["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"number","children":"01 / DEFINE"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Make the boundary testable."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Identify tools, permissions, data and autonomy. Define the organisation's risk tolerance and red lines. Decide how each material consequence will be observed."}]]}],["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"number","children":"02 / CHALLENGE"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Introduce a realistic failure."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Exercise cyber, operational and agentic scenarios in an authorised test environment. Separate attempted actions from realised impact."}]]}],["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"number","children":"03 / REPEAT"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Test the control change."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"After customer remediation, restore the starting conditions and rerun the same scenario. Record what changed and what remains unresolved."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"editorial","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WORKED EXAMPLES"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":["Follow a failure",["$","br",null,{}],"all the way through."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"A malicious document. A lost acknowledgement. A missing approval. Explore how each could turn into a consequential action, and which control to test."}],["$","a",null,{"className":"link-line","href":"/scenarios/","children":"Explore test scenarios ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"product-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE PLANNED OUTPUT"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":["Tested Operating",["$","br",null,{}],"Conditions."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"A record of the configuration, autonomy and controls under which the assessed agent stayed within stated risk tolerance across the scenarios actually tested."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Independent control verification refers to the controls being assessed. It does not mean independence from Cybernetic Limited or accredited certification."}],["$","a",null,{"className":"button outline","href":"/evidence/","children":"Inside the evidence pack ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"boundary","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE LIMIT OF THE CLAIM"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"A test result is evidence. It is not a guarantee."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Results apply to the configuration, environment and scenarios assessed. Untested areas, unresolved failures and inconclusive results belong in the conclusion. The organisation remains responsible for risk acceptance."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"RiskStriker is in development. Initial scope excludes production runtime defence, automatic remediation and certification."}]]}]]
